data.what-the-agent-sees#What the agent sees:
The agent gets one tool per saved request. Tool names use only letters, digits, _ and -, so get user becomes get_user. The tool’s arguments are the request’s fillable placeholders: the placeholders that neither the environment nor the collection defines. For get-user above, that is just id.
{"name": "get-user", "arguments": {"id": "42"}} The result is the run --json object, with isError set when ok is false. Secrets are masked everywhere in it, including response bodies that echo them back:
{"ok":true,"status":200,"url":"https://api.example.com/users/42","body":{"id":"42","auth":"Bearer *****"}}

data.--reveal#--reveal:
--reveal (on show, list, codegen, paste, env show) prints the literal values for a human at a terminal.
Revealed values end up in terminal scrollback, clipboard history (paste --reveal) and generated files (codegen --reveal). Never use --reveal in CI or in a session an AI agent can read. It is refused in agent mode with exit code 2:
{"ok":false,"error":"--reveal is not allowed in agent mode"}
